ChatGPT said:
In our Jenkins pipeline setup, we use the MSBuild pipeline plugin to build both traditional MSBuild and .NET Core projects by setting the enableDotnetCore parameter to true or false. Many of these projects also include Node.js modules—for frontend applications or utilities—which need to be built and tested as part of the process. Earlier, we handled this by integrating Node build and test steps directly within the MSBuild pipeline. However, in the simplified approach, we’ve separated the Node and MSBuild/.NET build processes into independent pipelines and connected them using pipeline chaining. This makes the system more modular, easier to maintain, and allows better reuse and flexibility in managing builds.
